 **Exercise + light therapy + social contact** → triple protective effect, 85% correlation with \"good days\"\n8. **Month Oct-Feb** → baseline 2-point mood reduction compared to May-Aug\n9. **SI progression pattern:** passive → active-no-plan often preceded by 2+ days of isolation + alcohol\n\n### Edge Cases and Challenges\n\n1. **Crisis detection:** The model should alert when SI progresses beyond \"passive.\" This requires careful handling and safety protocols.\n\n2. **Seasonal baseline:** January mood of \"5\" is actually better than her January average. The model should compare to seasonal baseline, not annual.\n\n3. **Medication lag:** If she starts a new medication, it takes 4-6 weeks to work. Short-term correlations are misleading.\n\n4. **Hypersomnia vs healthy sleep:** Sleeping 10 hours looks like \"good sleep\" but is actually a depression symptom. The model needs to flag excessive sleep.\n\n5. **Academic calendar interaction:** Her symptoms worsen in grading season (December, May) layered on top of seasonal pattern.\n\n---\n\n## Scenario 13: SIBO (Small Intestinal Bacterial Overgrowth)\n\n### User Profile\n**Name:** Lisa, 37, Accountant  \n**Condition:** SIBO (hydrogen-dominant), post-antibiotic treatment, on elemental diet transition  \n**Goals:** Successfully reintroduce foods, identify remaining triggers, prevent relapse\n\n### Items Tracked\n\n| Name | Type | Value Type | Unit | Options |\n|------|------|------------|------|---------|\n| Food reintroduction item | input | text | - | - |\n| Portion size | input | select | - | tiny, small, medium, normal |\n| Prokinetic taken | input | boolean | - | - |\n| Digestive enzyme taken | input | boolean | - | - |\n| Meal spacing | input | number | hours | - |\n| Fermented foods | input | select | - | none, small-amount, moderate |\n| Prebiotic foods | input | boolean | - | - |\n| Fasting hours overnight | input | number | hours | - |\n| Stress level | context | scale | 1-10 | - |\n| Sleep hours | context | number | hours | - |\n| Days since antibiotic | context | number | days | - |\n| Bloating | output | scale | 0-10 | - |\n| Bloating timing | output | select | - | none, immediate, 30min, 1-2hr, 3-4hr, next-day |\n| Gas frequency | output | select | - | minimal, moderate, frequent, constant |\n| Abdominal distension | output | boolean | - | - |\n| Stool type | output | select | - | Bristol 1-7 |\n| Brain fog | output | scale | 0-10 | - |\n| Histamine symptoms | output | boolean | - | - |\n| Fatigue | output | scale | 0-10 | - |\n\n### Sample Week of Entries (Week 3 of Reintroduction)\n\n**Monday:**\n- Reintro: zucchini, Portion: tiny, Prokinetic: true, Enzyme: true\n- Meal spacing: 4hr, Fermented: none, Prebiotic: false, Fasting: 14hr\n- Stress: 3, Sleep: 7, Days since abx: 21\n- Bloating: 2, Timing: none, Gas: minimal, Distension: false, Stool: 4, Fog: 1, Histamine: false, Fatigue: 3\n\n**Tuesday:**\n- Reintro: zucchini, Portion: small, Prokinetic: true, Enzyme: true\n- Meal spacing: 5hr, Fermented: none, Prebiotic: false, Fasting: 14hr\n- Stress: 3, Sleep: 7.5, Days since abx: 22\n- Bloating: 2, Timing: none, Gas: minimal, Distension: false, Stool: 4, Fog: 1, Histamine: false, Fatigue: 2\n\n**Wednesday:**\n- Reintro: zucchini + chicken, Portion: small, Prokinetic: true, Enzyme: true\n- Meal spacing: 4hr, Fermented: none, Prebiotic: false, Fasting: 13hr\n- Stress: 4, Sleep: 6.5, Days since abx: 23\n- Bloating: 3, Timing: 1-2hr, Gas: moderate, Distension: false, Stool: 4, Fog: 2, Histamine: false, Fatigue: 3\n\n**Thursday:**\n- Reintro: garlic (trace in chicken), Portion: tiny, Prokinetic: true, Enzyme: true\n- Meal spacing: 5hr, Fermented: none, Prebiotic: false, Fasting: 14hr\n- Stress: 5, Sleep: 7, Days since abx: 24\n- Bloating: 6, Timing: 30min, Gas: frequent, Distension: true, Stool: 5, Fog: 4, Histamine: false, Fatigue: 5\n\n**Friday:**\n- Reintro: none (recovery day), Portion: n/a, Prokinetic: true, Enzyme: true\n- Meal spacing: 5hr, Fermented: none, Prebiotic: false, Fasting: 16hr\n- Stress: 4, Sleep: 7, Days since abx: 25\n- Bloating: 4, Timing: 1-2hr, Gas: moderate, Distension: false, Stool: 5, Fog: 3, Histamine: false, Fatigue: 4\n\n**Saturday:**\n- Reintro: rice (well-cooked), Portion: small, Prokinetic: true, Enzyme: true\n- Meal spacing: 4hr, Fermented: none, Prebiotic: false, Fasting: 14hr\n- Stress: 2, Sleep: 8, Days since abx: 26\n- Bloating: 2, Timing: none, Gas: minimal, Distension: false, Stool: 4, Fog: 1, Histamine: false, Fatigue: 2\n\n**Sunday:**\n- Reintro: rice + salmon, Portion: medium, Prokinetic: true, Enzyme: true\n- Meal spacing: 5hr, Fermented: small-amount, Prebiotic: false, Fasting: 13hr\n- Stress: 2, Sleep: 8, Days since abx: 27\n- Bloating: 3, Timing: 1-2hr, Gas: moderate, Distension: false, Stool: 4, Fog: 2, Histamine: true, Fatigue: 3\n\n### Correlations Engine Might Discover\n\n1. **Any garlic, even trace** → 90% correlation with bloating >5 within 30 minutes (fructan intolerance)\n2. **Meal spacing <4 hours** → 45% increased bloating (incomplete migrating motor complex)\n3. **Overnight fasting >14 hours** → 30% improvement in morning symptoms (gut-clearing)\n4. **Fermented foods** → variable response, may trigger histamine symptoms\n5. **New food + small portion** → safe threshold; medium portion same day → 60% reaction risk\n6. **Stress >5** → 50% correlation with slower gastric emptying and increased symptoms\n7. **Prokinetic skipped** → 40% more likely to have next-day symptoms\n8. **Prebiotic foods too early** → 85% correlation with relapse symptoms within 72 hours\n\n### Edge Cases and Challenges\n\n1. **Cross-contamination tracking:** The garlic reaction came from garlic powder in seasoning, not obvious garlic. Need \"hidden ingredient\" notation.\n\n2. **Cumulative load:** Each food alone is fine, but 3 \"small\" portions in one day exceeds her tolerance. Need daily load calculation.\n\n3. **Reintroduction protocol:** Foods should be introduced one at a time over 3 days. The model should warn if protocol is rushed.\n\n4. **Symptom timing precision:** \"1-2hr\" bloating timing suggests small intestine, while \"next-day\" suggests large intestine. This distinction matters for identifying fermentation location.\n\n5. **Relapse detection:** If symptoms gradually increase over 2 weeks, SIBO may be returning. Need trend alerts.\n\n---\n\n## Scenario 14: Menopause Transition\n\n### User Profile\n**Name:** Diane, 51, School Principal  \n**Condition:** Perimenopause (2 years), not on HRT due to breast cancer family history  \n**Goals:** Manage hot flashes, improve sleep, stabilize mood swings\n\n### Items Tracked\n\n| Name | Type | Value Type | Unit | Options |\n|------|------|------------|------|---------|\n| Black cohosh supplement | input | boolean | - | - |\n| Phytoestrogen foods | input | select | - | none, some, focused |\n| Evening primrose oil | input | boolean | - | - |\n| Spicy food | input | boolean | - | - |\n| Alcohol units | input | number | units | - |\n| Caffeine mg | input | number | mg | - |\n| Bedroom temperature | input | number | °F | - |\n| Moisture-wicking sleepwear | input | boolean | - | - |\n| Exercise minutes | input | number | minutes | - |\n| Sleep hours | context | number | hours | - |\n| Work stress | context | scale | 1-10 | - |\n| Days since last period | context | number | days | - |\n| Hot flash count | output | number | count | - |\n| Hot flash severity | output | scale | 1-10 | - |\n| Night sweats | output | number | count | - |\n| Sleep disruption | output | number | times-woken | - |\n| Mood stability | output | scale | 1-10 | - |\n| Anxiety | output | scale | 0-10 | - |\n| Vaginal dryness | output | scale | 0-10 | - |\n| Joint pain | output | scale | 0-10 | - |\n\n### Sample Week of Entries\n\n**Monday:**\n- Black cohosh: true, Phytoestrogen: focused, EPO: true, Spicy: false\n- Alcohol: 0, Caffeine: 100, Bedroom: 66, Wicking: true, Exercise: 30\n- Sleep: 6, Stress: 6, Days since period: 45\n- Hot flashes: 4, Severi